.TH WINCAN 5 "November 2026" "wincan" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
wincan.ini \- settings of wincan
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B %APPDATA%\\wincan\\wincan.ini
is a Windows INI file that the program writes when the window is moved and at exit.  It can be edited while the program is not running.
.SS [wincan]
.TP
.B server
.RI [ https:// ] HOST:PORT
of the candle supply (default localhost:8766).  With
.B https://
the connection is encrypted and wincan proves who it is with the key named by
.BR client_cert ;
plain
.I HOST:PORT
is plain HTTP, for a loopback address.
.TP
.B client_cert
the SHA\-1 thumbprint (40 hexadecimal digits) of the certificate in the user's personal certificate store (CurrentUser\\My) that wincan shows to an https:// server.  The Windows installer makes the key and writes this; for a key made by hand, in PowerShell:
.PP
.nf
New\-SelfSignedCertificate \-Subject "CN=wincan client" \-KeyAlgorithm ECDSA_nistP256 \e
    \-KeyExportPolicy NonExportable \-CertStoreLocation Cert:\eCurrentUser\eMy
.fi
.PP
(with the client authentication usage); the thumbprint it prints is the value of client_cert.
The private key stays in the store.  \fBwincan \-\-fingerprint\fR prints the certificate's SHA\-256 fingerprint, which the server's administrator authorizes (\fBcandled \-\-authorize\fR).
.TP
.B key_prompt
1 (the default) offers to make a key at the start when the server is https:// and there is none; 0 once the offer has been declined.
.TP
.B server_pin
.TQ
.B server_pin_for
the SHA\-256 fingerprint of the server's certificate (\fBSHA256:\fR and 64 hexadecimal digits, as \fBcandled \-\-gen\-cert\fR printed it) and the server it is for.  A server whose certificate is another is refused.  If there is none, the first contact sets it and says so once (trust on first use); to change the server's certificate, remove these two lines.
.TP
.B pair
the coin shown (default BTC).
.TP
.B tf
the timeframe: 1m 3m 5m 15m 30m 1h 4h 1d or 1w (default 5m).
.TP
.B scale
the size of the window in percent (75 to 400, default 100 = 300 by 175 pixels).
.TP
.B fullscale
the magnification of the text in full screen, in percent (75 to 400, default 200); + and \- change it while in full screen.
.TP
.B x, y
the position of the window on the screen (the top left corner of the screen the first time, and whenever hardly any of the window, less than 60 by 40 pixels, would be on a screen at the saved place; it may be partly off the screen).
.TP
.B editfield
the box (0 to 3) that e opens the position editor on: the one last edited.
.TP
.B bollinger, ma9, ma200
1 or 0: whether each indicator is drawn (default 1).
.TP
.B volcandles
1 or 0: whether the candles are drawn with a width in proportion to their volume (default 0: standard candles).
.SS [positions]
One line for each coin that has a position:
.I NAME=ENTRY,SIZE
with the entry price, the size in coins (negative for a short), the time opened (Unix seconds), the leverage and the realized profit or loss in dollars, for example
.BR BTC=61000,0.5,1795160000,10,15 .  The last three may be missing.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wincan (1),
.BR candled (8)
